      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BELLA DANZA (9) showed good improvement in her second outing for the Grimson yard here a fortnight ago, sticking on for second in a Listed race behind accomplished mare Lux Aeterna. Has to overcome a wide barrier but she has the gate speed to do so and is suited coming back in grade. She could be ready to strike. SPARKLING SEA (4) makes her first appearance since July's Queensland Oaks but she was readied with a nice trial. Has won six of seven attempts at this circuit and distance and is unbeaten when fresh so expect a big return. FARFALLA STRIDE (7) made a good return when runner-up last week. Draws wider but is back against the girls and has won two of three previous second-up attempts so can progress. ALFNALMA (8) cops a wider draw but her recent consistency is hard to knock.",
